    {
      "dom_id": "question-83853",
      "name": null,
      "problem": "Which of the following differential equations is a logistic growth equation?",
      "worked_solution": "A logistic growth equation has the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dt}=ky(a-y),\n$$\n\nwhere $k>0$ is a constant of proportionality, and $a>y$ is the carrying capacity.\n\nFrom the given options, the only logistic growth equation is\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dt}=3y-4{y}^{2}.\n$$\n\nTo see this, let's factor the right-hand side of the equation. This gives,\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dt}=4y(\\frac{3}{4}-y).\n$$\n\nFrom here, we see that the constant of proportionality is $k=4,$ and the carrying capacity is $a=\\frac{3}{4}.$",
